  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Biology A.S. Degree - Local GE' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published September 4, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7631/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: SCC Local AA/AS. Official Total Units: 60-63; this seed models the path = 14 + 15 + 17 + 14 = 60 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page). Semester sums verified against the map's 14-15 / 15-17 / 17 / 14 headers. Judgment call — major path selection: the map offers an Allied Health Path (CHEM 305/309/400 in Sem 1; BIOL 430, 431 & 440 recommended) and a General Biology & Pre-Med Path (CHEM 400 in Sem 1; BIOL 402, 412 & 422 recommended). The General Biology & Pre-Med path is modeled here because it is the only fully prereq-coherent reading of the printed semester structure: with CHEM 305 in Sem 1 (the first-listed option), the Sem 4 List B slot (5 units, 'not already completed') has no satisfiable 5-unit option (BIOL 402/412/422 require CHEM 400 or BIOL 402; BIOL 430/431 would already be completed via List A; BIOL 440 is 4 units, breaking the printed 14-unit semester total), whereas the Gen Bio/Pre-Med chain CHEM 400 -> BIOL 402 -> BIOL 412 -> BIOL 422 is fully in-plan and matches every printed total. Choice slots: (1) ENGL C1000 / ENGL H+ 488 / ESLW 340, Local Area L1A — ENGL C1000 selected; (2) INDIS 313 / HCD 310, Local Area L7B Life Development Skills — INDIS 313 selected; (3) CHEM 305 / 309 / 400 Introduction to Chemistry (5), Local Area L5 — CHEM 400 selected per the General Biology & Pre-Med path (documented above); (4) Math: 'Choose one of the recommended courses under your STEM placements' (check eServices) — modeled as 'Any Local Area L2 course'; (5) Major Elective (List A) — a minimum of 10 units from BIOL 402, 412, 422, 430, 431 (choose one this semester, then one not already completed): BIOL 402 selected Sem 2, BIOL 412 selected Sem 3; (6) Major Elective (List B) — a minimum of 8 units from the List B course list (choose one this semester, then one not already completed to complete 8 units): BIOL 302 (3) selected Sem 3, BIOL 422 (5) selected Sem 4. In-plan prereqs: BIOL 402 requires CHEM 400 or equivalent college-level course with 'C' or better; BIOL 412 and BIOL 422 require BIOL 402 with 'C' or better (can be taken in either order) — all satisfied in-plan. Documented prereqs for the Allied Health path (not selected): CHEM 400 requires CHEM 300 within one year or ACS placement AND Intermediate Algebra; CHEM 305 requires Elementary Algebra (Integrated Math 1) 'C-' or better or concurrent MATHS 10; CHEM 309 requires Elementary Algebra 'C-' or better; BIOL 430 requires CHEM 305, 309, or 400; BIOL 431 requires BIOL 430; BIOL 434 requires BIOL 431; BIOL 440 requires CHEM 305, 309, 400 or equivalent; BIOL 362 requires BIOL 305 or equivalent. Full List B (minimum 8 units): BIOL 302 (3), 305 (4), C1001 (3), C1001L (1), 314 (3), 315 (1), 320 (3), 326 (3), 327 (1), 330 (3), 332 (4), 342 (3), 350 (3), 360 (3), 362 (4), 364 (2), 370 (4), 402 (5), 412 (5), 422 (5), 430 (5), 431 (5), 434 (3), 440 (4). Placement prereqs (documented): students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo; ENGL 488 requires ESL 325 with a 'C' or better; ESLW 340 requires ESL 325 or Los Rios assessment placement. 'This map is created based on catalog requirements. Many of the major elective requirements have prerequisites. Please see an SCC counselor.' AA requirements: 60 degree-applicable units with 2.0 GPA, 12 units within Los Rios, each required course 'C' or better, SCC local GE Areas L1A, L1B, L2, L3, L4, L5, L6, L7A, L7B. Electives: any courses numbered 100-499. Science, Math, & Engineering Meta Majors. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
